// The Starmap tab: the org database as a living 3D galaxy.
//
// Every heading is a star, every file a hub the headings in it hang off, every
// link a thread of light, and the outline - which org has and no other tool of
// this kind does - the faint structure that holds the whole picture together.
// Folders (or files) become coloured constellations named on tilted orbital
// rings. Archived things fall into a black hole that bends the light behind it.
//
// The split of labour here is the important part. `starmap/engine.ts` owns the
// canvas, the tooltip and the caption, because those three move at frame rate and
// nothing that moves at frame rate can go through React state. This file owns
// everything that changes when somebody does something: the toolbar, the search,
// the legend, the timeline and the panel. The engine tells it what it needs to
// know through callbacks, and each of those fires on a change rather than on a
// frame.
//
// The sliders write straight into the engine's live settings object - so dragging
// one costs no render at all - and are written back to the browser's settings
// debounced.

