// Editing an org file's text, from the Files tab's Org view.
//
// The Org view (OrgSource.tsx) is for reading and stays read only; the Edit
// button swaps this in over it. It is CodeMirror 6, coloured by the same line
// tokenizer the Org view uses (lineTokens), so a file looks the same either
// side of the button, with one of two sets of keys from the settings menu
// (`editorKeys`): vim (the default, @replit/codemirror-vim) or a small set of
// emacs ones written here.
//
// Three org things on top of a plain editor:
//
// 1. `<s TAB` and the rest of org-tempo's table (orgedit.ts) expand into a
//    block, with fields to step through: TAB to the next, shift-TAB back, TAB
//    off the last one to leave. The expansion only fires with nothing but
//    indentation before the `<`, as org-tempo's does.
// 2. `<c TAB` opens a menu of the server's capture templates. The one picked is
//    written in place (not filed where the template says) as fields stepped
//    through the same way; ESC at any point takes the whole thing back out.
// 3. Saving sends the text the editor started from as well, and the server
//    refuses when the file has changed since (a capture, a kanban drag, Emacs),
//    so a save cannot silently throw somebody else's write away.
//
// Fields are tracked in a StateField and mapped through every change, greedy
// at both ends so text typed at either edge of a field goes into it. Two
// fields with one key are one value written twice: the first is typed into
// and a transaction filter copies it to the rest.

