// The pieces the two layouts of a board share.
//
// A board can be drawn as columns of cards or as one grouped list, and the
// things that are the same either way live here rather than in one of them:
// how a date is said, what a priority is coloured, and what a heading looks
// like opened up. A row of the list opened and a card turned over are the same
// question asked twice, and answering it in two places is how they drift.

