// The Refactor tab: four structural changes to the outline, each shown as a
// diff before anything is written.
//
//   Rename a tag      across every file (or a query's headings): headline tags,
//                     FILETAGS and #+TAGS; a name already in use is a merge;
//                     or take a tag off everything.
//   Split to file     a heading and its subtree into a new file, a link left
//                     where it was.
//   Merge headings    one heading's text, children, tags and properties into
//                     another.
//   List to headings  a list in a heading's text into child headings.
//
// Every operation is a preview first (POST /refactor/<op>/preview), drawn per
// file with the Diff tab's own viewer, and then an apply that carries the
// preview's token: if a file changed in between, the server refuses and the
// page offers to preview again rather than writing a change nobody saw.
//
// Logic is in src/refactor.ts (tested), requests in src/refactorApi.ts. The
// command palette opens the tab on one operation (requestRefactorOp).

